---
# Postmortem Plugin Configuration
# Copy this file to your project's .claude/postmortem.local.md and customize

# Storage directory for postmortem documents (relative to project root)
storage_dir: ".claude/postmortem"

# Commit filtering settings
commit_filter:
  # Commit types to exclude (only used when include_keywords is not set)
  # Common conventional commit types
  exclude_types:
    - "feat"
    - "docs"
    - "chore"
    - "style"
    - "refactor"
    - "test"
    - "build"
    - "ci"
    - "perf"

  # Keywords to include in commit messages
  # If set, ONLY commits containing these keywords will be analyzed
  # If not set, all commits except exclude_types will be analyzed
  # Uncomment to enable:
  # include_keywords:
  #   - "fix"
  #   - "bug"
  #   - "hotfix"
  #   - "patch"
  #   - "resolve"
  #   - "issue"

# Postmortem generation settings
postmortem:
  # Minimum severity to generate postmortem (low, medium, high, critical)
  min_severity: "low"

  # Automatically generate tags from commit content
  auto_tag: true

  # Include full diff in postmortem document
  include_diff: false

  # Batch size for processing commits during init/update
  batch_size: 20

# Severity level definitions (for reference)
# - critical: System crash, data loss, security breach
# - high: Core functionality broken, widespread impact
# - medium: Feature broken, workaround available
# - low: Minor issue, edge case, cosmetic problem
---

Postmortem plugin configuration template.

Copy this file to your project's `.claude/postmortem.local.md` to customize settings for your project.
